{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789488294,"nonce":"QQLQh9lWN4qC+do+QTBXUQaqvNg=","title":"The release analysis re-derives every function's returned parameters each round","message":"`ModuleFacts::build` asked `functions_returning_params` for every non-external function on every round of its fixed point, and for each parameter of each function scanned the whole value table for the parameter's values before tracing them: about 2.5 ms over 195 functions in three rounds on bench_pipeline, on every run.\n\nNow: a function returning nothing, or only scalars, answers without tracing; the parameter values are collected in one pass; and after the first round only the callers of whoever changed are asked again (`callees_of` inverted once, shared with the owned-returning fixed point). Measured on the M1 Pro under load: returns_param 2.5 to 1.0 ms on bench_pipeline, the facts as a whole 4.3 to 2.3; bench_records 2.7 to 1.8.\n\nLeft: the owned-returning pass still walks every function once (about 1.1 ms), and both are recomputed over the library on every run because the program's hooks feed into the library's facts (a snapshot cannot carry them as they are).","files":null}]}